    <div class="post-container" id="fpc-2505086">
                      
		<div class="post" id="post-2505086">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,2505086)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-2505086">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/hercules-rockefeller" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2314402); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2314402&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608349761" alt="Hercules Rockefeller" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2314402)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/hercules-rockefeller" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2314402); return false;" >Hercules Rockefeller</a></span> <span class="odate time_1462667119 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 May 2016 00:25</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2505086">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;thoughts</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;thoughts</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I thought you handled it fine.</p>
<p>I wasn't saying you shouldn't deal with sensitive subject matter, and I wasn't offended by what you wrote. My criticism was purely from a writing perspective - I felt like the inclusion of details about the murder, and the mention that she had been raped, were unnecessary, plot-wise:<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-883846-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-883846-1')">1</a></sup> the mere fact that she'd been murdered seemed to me more than enough to make us hate Harold Maine, and to set in motion whatever it is that will happen next. Because child murder and rape tend to elicit such powerful, knee-jerk-type reactions in people, I just tend to think they should be used sparingly, otherwise you can end up with something that's over-the-top and overly dramatic (not that I thought that was the case here, mind you).</p>
<p>When I said those details felt like they'd been added for shock value, I wasn't saying that's why I thought <em>you</em> did it, I just meant that's what it <em>felt</em> like (I realize I should have expressed myself more clearly - sorry about that). And after reading your reasons for including those details, it's even clearer to me that you weren't using them simply to shock readers (and now that you say the rape <em>is</em> necessary for later on, my whole argument might be moot&#8230;)</p>
<p>And really, I'm not even that opposed to your inclusion of those details - it was simply a small criticism I had, based on my own personal tastes. Let me reiterate that I thought the tale was otherwise beautifully written, horrific, heart-wrenching and quite powerful. I'm looking forward to the continuation of the series. :)</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
